<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna restart consistency, P0 restart machinery: what a function prints
    must not depend on whether its analysis restarted.  A restarted pass
    starts from the prototype store the drive gave the first pass
    (infra/decompile_drive.rs (run_pipeline)), and `returndup auto` reads the
    returned register off the RETURN op (p8_structure/kuna_o0returns.rs
    (groups)).

    gcc 11 -O0 (-fno-pic -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none) of
        int pick(int c)
        {
            int ret = -1;
            switch (c) {
            case 'e': ret = 2; break;
            case 'i': ret = 0; break;
            case 'o': ret = 1; break;
            }
            return ret;
        }
    The cases jump to the epilogue, which loads ret itself (mov eax,[rbp-4]),
    so the function has one return statement.  By default `loweredswitch`
    records the compare cascade and restarts the function to install the
    switch; the restarted pass used to see the prototype store the first pass
    attached, whose output the restart had cleared, so the epilogue read as
    not computing eax and was split into one `return K;` per case.  An
    installed switch stays for the rest of a session, so the bytes are loaded
    twice and pass 2 reads the copy at 0x200000.

    Pass 1 (default): pick prints the switch (#1) with its cases breaking to
    one return of the frame slot (#2, #3).  Pass 2 (option loweredswitch off,
    no restart): pick_off keeps its tests (#4) and returns the frame slot
    from the same one statement (#3).  Neither pass splits the epilogue (#5).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">554889e5897decc745fcffffffff837dec6f7426837dec6f7f28837dec657408837dec69740beb1ac745fc02000000eb11c745fc00000000eb08c745fc01000000908b45fc5dc3</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x200000" readonly="true">554889e5897decc745fcffffffff837dec6f7426837dec6f7f28837dec657408837dec69740beb1ac745fc02000000eb11c745fc00000000eb08c745fc01000000908b45fc5dc3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="pick"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x200000" name="pick_off"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu pick</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option loweredswitch off</com>
  <com>lo fu pick_off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="RESTARTPROTO #1: pick's cascade prints as a switch (pass 1)" min="1" max="1">^  switch\(a0\) \{$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="RESTARTPROTO #2: pick's cases break to the shared return (pass 1)" min="2" max="2">^      break;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="RESTARTPROTO #3: each function returns its frame slot once (pass 1, pass 2)" min="2" max="2">^  return v1;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="RESTARTPROTO #4: with loweredswitch off pick_off keeps its tests (pass 2)" min="1" max="1">^ +if \(a0 == 0x69\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="RESTARTPROTO #5: no epilogue is split (pass 1, pass 2)" min="0" max="0">return-dupe</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
